I finally did it... ascended. Granted, Bar-Hum-Mal-Cha isn't too hard
to ascend (compared to other things like Tourist or Healer), but it was
a major victory for me, never having ascended anything before.

This guy started out with a battle axe and a short sword, so I ditched
the sword early on. Lost my pet to a falling rock trap in Dlvl 2. 
Oops. I found Gauntlets of Dexterity and Speed Boots early on, and
once I hit level 7, that gave me a significant advantage. I went to
Sokoban first, cleared it out, and got "oR. I was somewhat distressed,
because I was rapidly becoming unable to lug around all the cool stuff
I had, due to inventory letter space coming to a premium. "No problem,"
I thought, "I'll find a BoH or at least a sack in Minetown." After
making it there, however, I was disappointed to find only a bag of
tricks. No sack, no BoH, nothing. This trend would continue until about
Dlvl 16 or so, when a monster finally dropped a sack. However, the mine
town altar was coaligned, so I used the BoT to get Cleaver. Since I was
expert in battle axes, Cleaver was a help to my early game. I stopped
sacrificing after this and went down to clear out the rest of the
mines. Found a luckstone a little before Mine's End, and with the con-
stant problem of no room in my backpack, I settled for looting the
!oBooze in the wine cellar (my flavor of Mine's End) and going back up.
(This would come in handy on the Planes later.)

I ended up putting all my extraneous stuff in a box at the beginning
of the mines. I would come back here many times to dump and retrieve
things. I trodded down the dungeon, rapidly descending and clearing out
the levels. The Rogue level contained my quest transporter, which was
amusing. I hadn't reached level 14 yet, so I kept going down. My AC was
about -15 at this point, thanks to dwarvish mithril, an enchanted shirt,
and a little enchantment on my speed boots. I suddenly hit the castle
level, and took a quick look at the occupants via telepathy. The liches
scared me and I turned tail and ran. Went back to an altar, made holy
water, and sacrificed madly to get crowned. Stormy was a friend for the
rest of the game, but he got a little too zealous and whacked the watch
captain in minetown, providing me with a silver sword. My AC was better
then, so I took off for the quest. The quest was fairly easy; a troll
dropped a /oDeath which I used to kill Thoth Amon before he could do
things to my armor. (Cowardly, yes, but I like it too.) As I climbed up
with the Heart of Ahriman, I came across a wand. I IDed it -- polymorph!
I took this, and a set of yellow dragon scales (where I got those, I
don't remember... most likely outside of the castle) and ran back to the
stash. I then realized I hadn't IDed charging yet, so I settled for
ditching my dwarven mithril in favor of YDSM (mostly for the AC drop.)
As I was sorting through the various scrolls I found, I managed to ID
b?oGenocide, so I genocided Ls, and forged down into the castle.

With a little /oCold + /oStriking action, the drawbridge fell and I
assaulted the occupants. They fell fairly handily to Stormy. I took the
/oWishing, and retreated again to the mine stash. Wished for 2b?oCharge,
SDSM, a blessed Bag of Holding, a [CoMR, a MM, [HoT, and wrested out a
=oSD. Polypiling my scrolls precipitated out more than enough ?oEA and
?oEW scrolls to lower my AC to -38 (after a little more protection) and
net me +7 Stormy and a +7 silver sabre, which would remain my weapons
for the rest of the game. I used the other two ?oGeno I found to geno-
cide h and ;, making my descent into Gehennom fairly uneventful. After
marking the vibrating square (with a lovely arrow made out of orcish
arrows) I ascended Rodney's tower, and a disenchanter was living in the
zoo. The bastard took two points off of the silver sabre! And me with a
dried up marker and no ?oEW. I nailed it with a wand and cursed its
family as it died. Rose up, and woke up Rodney, and wasted 5 charges
from my /oDeath just trying to kill him. He was a slippery rascal, but
I managed to hit him with the bolt and he broke. Grabbed the book, ran
like a little girl to the square, and barged into Moloch's high temple.
Up to this point, there were almost no times where my barbarian was
even close to dying. However, the combination of Moloch and the high
priest finally got me down very low, so I had to quaff a !oFH for the
first time in the game. (Thanks to Quietust from NAO for helping me with
the alchemy stuff, BTW.) Amulet in hand, named appropriately, I began
my ascension run. Rodney showed up again, but I put him down with the
/oDeath. Recharged the /oDeath, and went to the planes. Earth was no
problem, other than Rodney showing up again. The plane of Air kicked my
ass. I had to quaff three !oFH just to get out of there alive. It was
insane. Spent no time at all on the plane of Fire, and the plane of
Water was a bear because the portal kept moving. I found it, though,
and I ascended to the astral plane! And Death was RIGHT beside me! I
retreated to the left, and Death left me alone. Famine and I fought,
and while he did score a couple of effective hits on me while I strug-
gled to unload the /oDeath on him,  I eventually got it and killed him.
I ran to the altar, checked it -- damn! Neutral. I barged out, and
Famine reappeared -- no problem, another /oDeath charge. However, I was
running low, so I decided to withhold usage. Of course, as I step out
into the hallway, I'm rushed by an Archon. And to make matters worse,
Famine reappears. So, I put my guardian angel between Famine and
myself, and whale on the Archon with Stormy and the silver sabre. After
a !oFH and liberal unihorning, the Archon falls. Unfortunately, my angel
also falls, and I'm forced to take on Famine again. However, the angel
weakened Famine, so I rushed in head-long and introduced him to my twin
swords. Famine died and never got back up. I walked down the hallway
towards the right altar (wanting to avoid Death,) but Death's in the
hallway again. So, I put a vampire between me and him, and zap wands at
Death until he retreats out of the line of sight. Then, I snuck up and
smacked him a few times, and killed him. (Killed Death? Odd.) I check
the altar; it's chaotic. I sacrifice, the choir sings, and I drink a
beer in celebration! It was a very exciting and frustrating game,
having to do without the BoH and MM and whatnot for so long. It just
goes to show how powerful the /oWishing is.

Things I learned from this game:
1) Cleaver isn't that bad of an artifact for Barbarians to start out
with. It does a lot of damage to everything, and you're more than likely
already expert at battle-axes by the time you get it.

2) Stormbringer + silver sabre is an AWESOME #twoweapon combo. Most
level drain resistant monsters are vulnerable to silver, and the oppo-
site is usually true, too. 99% of the monsters you meet will suffer from
this combination.

3) The _ key is your friend for moving between levels.

4) Killing shopkeepers is a very easy way to net protection money. (No,
I left Izchak alone. ;p)

I'm proud to have ascended. It appears I've done a relatively quick
ascension, too, given by the comments I've recieved. I felt I wasted a
lot of time shuffling between the stash in the mines and wherever I
needed to be. (I stopped going back after I got to Gehennom, though.)
I hope I get to post some more YAAP posts some day!

